  "summary_en": "Singapore CSA's voluntary draft addendum to its Securing AI Systems Companion Guide, covering software-based agentic AI. It sets out a lifecycle, risk-based approach with threat modelling, taint tracing, autonomy levels, and controls such as least privilege, sandboxing, monitoring and human-in-the-loop, illustrated by three case studies.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Start with a risk assessment that assesses autonomy level (0-3) and maps workflows.",
   "Use taint tracing to track untrusted data and isolate tainted components.",
   "Controls across lifecycle: supply chain security, least privilege, environment segmentation, sandboxing.",
   "Continuous monitoring, logging, and human approval for high-risk or irreversible actions.",
   "Secure MCP servers and inter-agent (A2A) communication; voluntary and non-exhaustive."
